    <!-- How to use overlay -->
    <Border
      Grid.Row="0"
      Grid.RowSpan="9"
      Background="#ee1a1a2e"
      CornerRadius="8"
      Visibility="{Binding IsHowToUseVisible, Converter={StaticResource BoolToVis}}"
      Padding="20"
      VerticalAlignment="Stretch"
      HorizontalAlignment="Stretch"
    >
      <Border Background="{StaticResource CardBg}" CornerRadius="8" Padding="16">
        <Grid>
          <Grid.RowDefinitions>
            <RowDefinition Height="Auto" />
            <RowDefinition Height="*" />
            <RowDefinition Height="Auto" />
          </Grid.RowDefinitions>
          <TextBlock
            Grid.Row="0"
            Text="How to Use"
            FontSize="16"
            FontWeight="Bold"
            Foreground="{StaticResource TextPrimary}"
            Margin="0,0,0,12"
          />
          <ScrollViewer Grid.Row="1" VerticalScrollBarVisibility="Auto" Margin="0,0,0,12">
            <StackPanel>
            <TextBlock
              Foreground="{StaticResource TextSecondary}"
              FontSize="12"
              TextWrapping="Wrap"
              LineHeight="20"
              xml:space="preserve"
              Visibility="{Binding IsAccountsMode, Converter={StaticResource BoolToVis}}"
            >
              <Run
                FontWeight="SemiBold"
                Text="1. Setup"
              />
Place HearthSwing.exe anywhere you like. Open Settings and set the Game Path (folder with WowClassic.exe) and Saved Accounts Path (where saved account snapshots are stored).

<Run
                FontWeight="SemiBold"
                Text="2. Save an account"
              />
Click "Save Account" or "Review Save". HearthSwing scans the live WTF accounts. If the account has never been saved, it captures the full account snapshot. If it already exists, it shows account settings plus realm and character checkboxes, preselecting the slices that actually changed.

<Run
                FontWeight="SemiBold"
                Text="3. Switch accounts"
              />
Click a saved account button to apply that account snapshot into WTF. After switching, launch WoW and click Restore, then type /reload in the game to apply the restored cache files.

<Run
                FontWeight="SemiBold"
                Text="4. Launch WoW"
              />
Click "Launch WoW" to start the game with cache protection enabled. Cache files are locked read-only and restored from backup to prevent server sync from overwriting your local settings.

<Run
                FontWeight="SemiBold"
                Text="5. Cache protection"
              />
After launch, cache files stay locked for the configured delay (default 120s). Use "Unlock" to release early or "Restore" to force-restore from the active saved account while WoW is running (type /reload after).

<Run
                FontWeight="SemiBold"
                Text="6. Save on exit"
              />
If Save on Exit is enabled, HearthSwing compares the live account against the active saved snapshot when WoW closes. Auto-save writes changed account settings and characters immediately; otherwise the save review overlay opens so you can confirm the changed slices.

<Run
                FontWeight="SemiBold"
                Text="Note:"
              />
HearthSwing transfers macros, keybindings, edit mode layout, and addon settings. Action bars are NOT transferred. Use the ActionBarSaver addon (for TBC Anniversary: ActionBarSaver Reloaded) to save/restore action bars separately.</TextBlock
            >
            <TextBlock
              Foreground="{StaticResource TextSecondary}"
              FontSize="12"
              TextWrapping="Wrap"
              LineHeight="20"
              xml:space="preserve"
              Visibility="{Binding IsTemplatesMode, Converter={StaticResource BoolToVis}}"
            ><Run
                FontWeight="SemiBold"
                Text="Templates: what they are"
              />
Templates let you reuse one character's setup (macros, keybindings, edit mode, addon settings) across many characters, accounts and realms. There are two separate template types: Character templates and Account templates.

<Run
                FontWeight="SemiBold"
                Text="1. Character template"
              />
Click "Create Template", choose "Character", pick a donor character from the account/realm/character tree (use the search box to filter), give it a name, and Create. HearthSwing depersonalizes it, replacing the donor character and realm names with tokens so it can be reused anywhere.

<Run
                FontWeight="SemiBold"
                Text="2. Account template"
              />
Choose "Account" instead to capture only the shared account-level settings (account SavedVariables and account root files). Account templates are applied to a whole account and overwrite settings shared by every character on that account.

<Run
                FontWeight="SemiBold"
                Text="3. Apply a template"
              />
Click "Apply" on a template card. Character templates ask for a target character (tree + search); account templates ask for a target account. Applying restores the template files into WTF using the same file-swap mechanism as Restore. Type /reload in WoW afterwards.

<Run
                FontWeight="SemiBold"
                Text="4. Launch WoW and cache protection"
              />
The Launch WoW button on this tab works exactly like on the Accounts tab: it locks the cache files read-only to stop the server from overwriting your local settings. Use Unlock to release early.

<Run
                FontWeight="SemiBold"
                Text="5. Versions"
              />
Each template keeps its own version history (the "Versions" button on each card). Rename or Delete a template from its card.

<Run
                FontWeight="SemiBold"
                Text="Note:"
              />
Action bars are NOT transferred by templates. Use the ActionBarSaver addon to save/restore action bars separately.</TextBlock
            >
            </StackPanel>
          </ScrollViewer>
          <Button
            Grid.Row="2"
            Content="Close"
            Style="{StaticResource ActionBtn}"
            Background="{StaticResource TextSecondary}"
            Command="{Binding ToggleHowToUseCommand}"
            HorizontalAlignment="Right"
            MinWidth="80"
          />
        </Grid>
